{"answer": "**Summary of the \u201cBudget numbers\u201d thread (Q4 planning)**  \n\n| Message No. | Sender | Time (UTC) | Key points |\n|------------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n| **msg\u201110** | Alice Ander | 10:00 | Announces that the quarter\u20114 budget spreadsheet is now available. |\n| **msg\u201111** | Bobby | 10:01 | Points out the travel line\u2011item appears too high. |\n| **msg\u201112** | Carol Corte | 10:02 | Echoes Bobby\u2019s concern and asks if the off\u2011site expense can be trimmed. |\n| **msg\u201113** | Alice Ander | 10:03 | Replies that off\u2011site is already committed; suggests looking at contractor costs instead. |\n| **msg\u201114** | Bobby | 10:04 | Explains that contractor spend is mainly due to the migration project. |\n| **msg\u201115** | *You* | 10:05 | States you will pull a contractor breakdown tomorrow. |\n| **msg\u201116** | Carol Corte | 10:06 | Adds that tooling renewals will also hit Q4. |\n| **msg\u201117** | Bobby | 10:07 | Notes two renewals that could be downgraded. |\n| **msg\u201118** | Alice Ander | 10:08 | Requests that all proposals be posted to the thread by Thursday. |\n| **msg\u201119** | Carol Corte | 10:09 | Confirms she will submit a proposal, taking responsibility for tooling. |\n| **msg\u201120** | Bobby | 10:10 | Confirms he will focus on travel scenarios. |\n| **msg\u201121** | *You* | 10:11 | Says you will reconcile the numbers against the previous quarter. |\n\n**Take\u2011away points**\n\n1. **Budget focus areas identified** \u2013 travel, contractors (primarily the migration project), and tooling renewals.\n2. **Action items**  \n   * *You* \u2013 Pull contractor break\u2011down by tomorrow.  \n   * Carol \u2013 Draft a proposal on tooling renewal adjustments.  \n   * Bobby \u2013", "answer_hash": "d091d27b36ba9c20bb7f78f874488a761e14a660c4faa9a808801ed64dd2492f", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-52", "seq": 52, "task_id": "t6-budget-exhaustion", "truncated": false, "ts": 1066.0}
